      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Watering: NC State says tolerates infrequent watering but should not dry out fully; RHS only says sparingly in winter. Mapped to let_top_dry. Light conflict: NC State bright indirect indoors, RHS several hours of direct sun; kept the gentler one. Temperature: summer 21 to 27 C (both), winter NC State 10 to 16 C, RHS 13 to 16 C; kept the higher winter minimum. Size: NC State up to 2 ft tall and 3 ft spread, RHS 10 cm tall and up to 50 cm spread; NC State used. Severity 1 maps NC State low severity and the ASPCA article (stomach upset). Caution: the ASPCA lists generic Senecio species as more serious (liver damage) and the fetched article does not use the name Curio; a vet check would settle it. Growth rate: no page states it. Interval: NC State 'tolerates infrequent watering, never allow to dry out completely between waterings'; Missouri Botanical Garden 'allow roots to dry out between waterings, tolerates infrequent watering'; RHS 'sparingly in winter'. NC State and MBG pull in opposite directions (never fully dry vs dry out between), so 14 stays unconfirmed. Pot and season: 13 cm pot, growing season; winter comes from the rest-season factor. Dry and wet tolerance days: no source gives any, unchanged."
      },
